Z||000000||crystalgeek||07-27-2001||07:39 PM||||Hello, <BR>This is my first time posting, so please forgive me if I do anything wrong.<BR>I have an 86 fiero that USED to have the 4-banger in it.  At some point, someone put in the v-6, and I don't know if they left the original computer in there or not...I don't know if it is the same computer for both engines?  Anyways....this car was running great for the first couple of months I had it.  Then I parked it and didn't start it for about 3 months (I know..me bad).  So when I went to start it, the battery was fine, cranked over no problem, it just wouldn't start...<BR>I put a gallon of fresh gas in it...nothing.<BR>Then I checked for spark at the center point of the distibutor and there was nothing there.  What could have gone wrong in the time that it was sitting there?  It was running fine when I parked it....now there is no spark.<BR>I don't know where to begin at troubleshooting this problem...<BR>Thanks for any ideas...<P>------------------<BR>Thanks,<BR>Alex O<BR>"I'd give my right arm to be ambidextrous"||||reg||9
Z||000001||PBJ||07-27-2001||07:50 PM||||I would remove your disc cap and look at the contections between pick up coil and ignition module. If it is green (corroded) likely these both should be replaced.  Common problem of lack of spark on v6 fiero.||||reg||1
